# Backends

Each backend implements connect, send, cancel, permission reply, disconnect. Map wire events to the shared core event set. The TUI must not include protocol headers.

| Flag | Transport | Do not confuse with |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `cursor` | Spawn `cursor-sdk-bridge`, Connect HTTP/1.1 | `agent acp` |
| `codex` | WebSocket JSON-RPC (no `jsonrpc` field) | Codex ACP adapter |
| `acp` | JSON-RPC 2.0 JSONL stdio client | `tny acp` server |
| `openai` | `POST /v1/responses` SSE (`/chat/completions` via `wire_api:"chat"`) | Host tool loops |

```c
/* ❌ BAD — TUI paints Connect frames */
/* ✅ GOOD — backend emits TNY_EV_TEXT_DELTA / TNY_EV_PERM_REQ */
```

Drain host stderr. Shutdown: RPC/EOF, wait, kill. Pin protos and Codex schema to a release tag. Details: `docs/backends/`.
